{"actor": "agent:practice-analysis", "at": "2026-11-26T04:01:14Z", "data": {"about": "science-factory/mvp/gain.py and confront.py (the candidate gain estimate)", "evidence": {"path": "receipts/known-answers-without-screen.json", "sha256": "7a9591601166c819b970cc644b0d1f777707a5b3d813d0746e0a8edf79c4da4b"}, "id": "NOTE-001", "kind": "method", "sha": "286dc32f7c6f8c531787ef91afbe46400f3e16a737b19fb543287a651939ed75", "text": "Without a quality screen the gain is steered by degraded passes at low stage. In known-answer tests built on the real 2024 pass times and gauge record, one-signed faults on a quarter of the lowest-stage passes cut interval coverage to 67 percent and raised false refutation right at the difference that matters to 34 percent and false confirmation there to 9 percent (2000 test cases per setting). In the 2024 record itself one pass with a degraded quality flag, at the year's lowest stage, carries about two thirds of the residual sum of squares. Proposed and written into the plan: exclude passes with reach_q at or above 2 before pairing and report the count."}, "hash": "178158a26c058354182ebfdc6d466405a2bc764ace62d9cbf25196cc137495df", "kind": "note.raised", "prev": "ba9e3d31d732e1f7d7f0ea9a3f8a34622ac7ccf61bd9a687ea93658b8061492d", "seq": 3}
