NATIVE_TLS", "UV_NO_PROGRESS", "UV_RUN_RECURSION_DEPTH", "XDG_DATA_DIRS", "https_proxy", "no_proxy"], "exit": 0, "plan_sha": "e98a32b9a309124dcf52e3aad9da3438be4cc0b4e22af28e4b7599de557f16dd", "problem": null, "receipt_sha": "757d615b2a36c9cfedebc475239097c7e93d3700df40cde3d83e1b5fb2dc3053", "test": "working-data"}, "hash": "c8ae36af5cab090bfee01cf91260364d42275f2abeca90cc767297cb8c3eb487", "kind": "test.run", "prev": "a7797b716273c016b60b7f8a726d98287bb3640d3d1973b0f7933cbe191d12db", "seq": 5}
{"actor": "agent:practice-analysis", "at": "2026-11-26T04:02:30Z", "data": {"about": "hydrology/knowledge/recipes/swot-gauge-confrontation.md (mean error of the change and its interval)", "evidence": {"path": "receipts/known-answers.json", "sha256": "c739886cf26430a0ea9a4b6962229d2339d488f16d434177cf5b9f539918b12c"}, "id": "NOTE-002", "kind": "method", "sha": "cb97a010efd9740eca49b32a5f43e11687758ac04f6957788785f3fe6fbd5074", "text": "The mean error of the change is blind to gain. Its 95 percent interval contained zero in every one of 2000 known-answer test cases per setting at gains of 1.00 and 0.90 and under a 0.5 m per year drift, run through the unmodified executor. Algebraically the mean of the change errors is the last level difference minus the first, divided by the count, so it reads two passes; its reported spread is about six times its actual spread across test cases. An independent check found it responds only to a drift far larger than the noise. The change RMSD and correlation in the same recipe are unaffected. Proposed: amend the recipe to say what this score can and cannot detect, or replace it with the gain; the recipe is signed, so the amendment owes a re-signature."}, "hash": "d3281fea42f7b47e9b5939a94ebe737cad92fb26c6e1327fd114a0dc0b9da0dc", "kind": "note.raised", "prev": "c8ae36af5cab090bfee01cf91260364d42275f2abeca90cc767297cb8c3eb487", "seq": 6}
{"actor": "agent:practice-analysis", "at": "2026-11-26T04:02:30Z", "data": {"about": "hydrology/knowledge (validity domain for claim class variability, SWOT reach elevation against a gauge)", "evidence": null, "id": "NOTE-003", "kind": "missing", "sha": "1e6d00d036e65fdb8e6011e09d75e26cb2bf4a4d35c4308082415c9ff7a0785c", "text": "No signed validity domain governs this claim class for this product, region and period, so a finding would be unadjudicated and could not become stable. A domain needs authoritative sources; the seeder drafts it from sources the steward supplies."}, "hash": "64a83e9d3d24aa70003a5ac87db17981f7607df60361c111f51771a67f26bc2f", "kind": "note.raised", "prev": "d3281fea42f7b47e9b5939a94ebe737cad92fb26c6e1327fd114a0dc0b9da0dc", "seq": 7}
{"actor": "agent:practice-analysis", "at": "2026-11-26T04:02:30Z", "data": {"about": "hydrology/knowledge/computations (the confrontation with a gain)", "evidence": null, "id": "NOTE-004", "kind": "missing", "sha": "f733eb2b3a29cd727b604a30f2a3a434926c64a170c897b59c9f0d5182dfeea6", "text": "The confrontation is a recipe with a script. A finding must cite an attested computation whose receipt carries the computation file's hash and a data manifest stamp, so the method lands as one before any finding is drafted."}, "hash": "2da945719944aa86f56c07c3f4f00fcb77c9b40d6533f3866ac94b37fac80215", "kind": "note.raised", "prev": "64a83e9d3d24aa70003a5ac87db17981f7607df60361c111f51771a67f26bc2f", "seq": 8}
{"actor": "agent:practice-analysis", "at": "2026-11-26T04:02:30Z", "data": {"about": "hydrology/verification/fixtures/fetch_confrontation_fixtures.py (processing identifier)", "evidence": null, "id": "NOTE-005", "kind": "missing", "sha": "eadca91709b33db9b81c45b9fc15723b742995da29ad845bddc4b639759cb9c0", "text": "The fetch does not keep the processing identifier (crid). The bundle records that this collection changes baseline on 2025-04-28; a window that mixes baselines leaks an offset step into the gain. The planned opening declines a window without one identifier per pass, so the fetch must capture it and the 2024 fixture must be refreshed before the opening-path rehearsal can pass."}, "hash": "796cd3d4573c1129f89830fd6f501cb538dfbc7b324b5fc0e4a749e145abfad4", "kind": "note.raised", "prev": "2da945719944aa86f56c07c3f4f00fcb77c9b40d6533f3866ac94b37fac80215", "seq": 9}
{"actor": "agent:practice-analysis", "at": "2026-11-26T04:02:31Z", "data": {"about": "hydrology/.github/workflows/plugin-gate.yml (findings checker)", "evidence": null, "id": "NOTE-006", "kind": "missing", "sha": "cfa0a8a688e03a4c7bfca7e6b3d9791a5a6025d1c5e48e715e330e78e8d73be8", "text": "The findings checker is not run by this repository's merge checks, so a finding's form is checked by nothing until this work wires it in. The plan's finding-form rehearsal requires a rehearsal finding drafted from the 2024 receipt to pass it before the lock."}, "hash": "e969391e8e0c5dad470a052d604c1c665cc88eb854a834f3f03d2aafc8e92650", "kind": "note.raised", "prev": "796cd3d4573c1129f89830fd6f501cb538dfbc7b324b5fc0e4a749e145abfad4", "seq": 10}
{"actor": "agent:practice-analysis", "at": "2026-11-26T04:02:31Z", "data": {"about": "science-factory/mvp/gain.py (power under an unflagged gross error)", "evidence": {"path": "receipts/working-data.json", "sha256": "757d615b2a36c9cfedebc475239097c7e93d3700df40cde3d83e1b5fb2dc3053"}, "id": "NOTE-007", "kind": "method", "sha": "d5a1066a11bfb5ddd17b8edbec54abadb4195ee3411ddfdefbdbb600e3ec7122", "text": "After the quality screen, one pass the product does not flag (2024-03-26, residual +0.86 m) carries about 70 percent of the residual sum of squares in the 2024 record. The interval still covers (the required gross-error cases: coverage 0.93), but the rule's power to support a true claim falls from about 0.95 in a kind case to about 0.49 when such passes occur. Proposed for the method work: a robust estimator written into the plan, or a plan that states the power it has when a gross error is present. Found by the second review pass."}, "hash": "777d72ff94d62d7de43dbecccf500cf2abb9d1c903af836e9d4ba67cb5b84df7", "kind": "note.raised", "prev": "e969391e8e0c5dad470a052d604c1c665cc88eb854a834f3f03d2aafc8e92650", "seq": 11}
{"actor": "agent:practice-coordinating", "at": "2026-11-26T04:06:08Z", "data": {"change": "Third review round and its verification, the study tool and the procedure (procedure 0.7.0), in two rounds. First round: the lock binds every file a command names, read from the study directory, and everything Python could import beside them; the plan check requires the subject (pair), a dated window and four required criteria, and refuses unknown keys, a key given twice and more than one opening; a test case is two parts, the data and what was put in, and the method is given the data alone; the record of what has been opened is matched by log fingerprint; a verdict counts only after the finding, the signature names the finding by checksum, and the log check applies the locked rules to the run receipt again; the system trial's verdict is written to the study log; the lock binds the request and records the procedure's checksum; the scorecard check clean-opening is renamed no-failed-opening and lock-committed is added. Second round, after an independent verifier: every command in a plan is a launcher the tool knows ({python}, or uv run) followed by a script file that exists and is bound, and anything else is refused by the plan check; a rehearsal lists the files it needs under needs, which the tool looks for itself and the lock binds; commands and git run in an environment built from a short list of names, with further names only where a plan step lists them under passes_environment, and each run records the names it was given; power_to_refute_when_false can no longer be waived; the known-answer tests run the method in a process of its own that is given only the data, in shuffled batches, and keep what was put in, the seed and the scoring to themselves; the self-test check on an opening whose fetch exited 0 now exercises its guard, and four other checks that could pass for another reason were tightened.", "change_log": "change-log.jsonl", "problem_class": "the promise could be broken through what the study tool did not bind, check or record", "record_sha": "8613222b656788aec46fc8bd48dd251f0baf40b49046f904582a2ee5c365cf7b"}, "hash": "18a3b2993163a2099cb2439500b631737923730b217aeed1938dbb1a4d95c78e", "kind": "change.recorded", "prev": "777d72ff94d62d7de43dbecccf500cf2abb9d1c903af836e9d4ba67cb5b84df7", "seq": 12}
